<div class="calcpad-output">
 <!-- Exercises the #html, #markdown and #cpd parsing modes: raw HTML blocks, multi-line Markdown, mode nesting, inline conditions and macros. -->
 <style>
  .note {
        border-left: 3px solid #4a7;
        background: #f4f9f6;
        padding: 6px 10px;
        margin: 8px 0;
    }
    .note b { color: #275; }
    /* The "Markdown Elements - All" CSS snippet, which the report template omits.
       Tables go through thead/tbody so Calcpad's own tables are left alone. */
    blockquote {
        margin: 0.8em 0;
        padding: 2px 12px;
        border-left: 3px solid #99a;
        color: #445;
    }
    pre { background: #f6f6f6; border: 1pt solid #ddd; padding: 6px 10px; overflow-x: auto; }
    code { background: #f2f2f2; padding: 0 2px; }
    pre code { background: none; padding: 0; }
    table { border-collapse: collapse; margin: 1em 0; }
    thead th { background: #f0f0f0; border: 1pt solid #aaa; padding: 4px 8px; text-align: left; }
    tbody td { border: 1pt solid #ccc; padding: 4px 8px; }
    ul.contains-task-list { list-style: none; padding-left: 1.2em; }
    li.task-list-item input[type="checkbox"] { margin-right: 6px; }
    ins { text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-color: #4a7; }
    del { color: #888; }
    hr { border: 0; border-top: 1pt solid #ccc; margin: 1em 0; }
 </style>
 <div>
  <span id="top">
  </span>
 </div>
 <h1>Parse Modes</h1>
 <p>
  A
  <code>#markdown</code>
  block renders
  <strong>consecutive</strong>
  lines together, so paragraphs,
tables and nested lists all work.
 </p>
 <table>
  <thead>
   <tr>
    <th>Case</th>
    <th>Load</th>
    <th>Factor</th>
   </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
   <tr>
    <td>Dead</td>
    <td>5 kN</td>
    <td>1.35</td>
   </tr>
   <tr>
    <td>Live</td>
    <td>3 kN</td>
    <td>1.5</td>
   </tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
 <ul>
  <li>
   Ultimate limit state
   <ul>
    <li>1.35 G + 1.5 Q</li>
   </ul>
  </li>
  <li>
   Serviceability limit state
   <ul>
    <li>
     1.0 G + 1.0 Q
Hello from macro
    </li>
   </ul>
  </li>
 </ul>
 <p>
  Emphasis extras:
  <ins>inserted</ins>
  , H
  <sub>2</sub>
  O, x
  <sup>2</sup>
  ,
  <del>struck</del>
  and a bare URL
  <a href="https://calcpad-ce.org">https://calcpad-ce.org</a>
  — plus a task list:
 </p>
 <ul class="contains-task-list">
  <li class="task-list-item">
   <input checked="checked" disabled="disabled" type="checkbox"/>
   Raw HTML passes through:
   <b>bold</b>
  </li>
  <li class="task-list-item">
   <input disabled="disabled" type="checkbox"/>
   Still to check
  </li>
 </ul>
 <h3>Inputs</h3>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>G</var>
   = 5
   <i>kN</i>
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>Q</var>
   = 3
   <i>kN</i>
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>γ</var>
   <sub>G</sub>
   = 1.35
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>γ</var>
   <sub>Q</sub>
   = 1.5
  </span>
 </p>
 <h3>Design load</h3>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>E</var>
   <sub>d</sub>
   =
   <var>γ</var>
   <sub>G</sub>
   ·
   <var>G</var>
   +
   <var>γ</var>
   <sub>Q</sub>
   ·
   <var>Q</var>
   = 1.35 · 5
   <i>kN</i>
   + 1.5 · 3
   <i>kN</i>
   = 11.25
   <i>kN</i>
  </span>
 </p>
 <div class="note">
  <b>Note:</b>
  a
  <code>#cpd</code>
  block inside
  <code>#html</code>
  calculates,
    then
  <code>#end cpd</code>
  pops back to raw HTML.
  <p>
   <span class="eq">
    <var>A</var>
    = 2
    <i>m</i>
    · 3
    <i>m</i>
    = 6
    <i>m</i>
    <sup class="unit">2</sup>
   </span>
  </p>
  <p>
   <span class="eq">
    <var>q</var>
    =
    <span class="dvc">
     <var>E</var>
     <sub>d</sub>
     <span class="dvl">
     </span>
     <var>A</var>
    </span>
    =
    <span class="dvc">
     11.25
     <i>kN</i>
     <span class="dvl">
     </span>
     6
     <i>m</i>
     <sup class="unit">2</sup>
    </span>
    = 1.88
    <i>kPa</i>
   </span>
  </p>
 </div>
 <blockquote>
  <p>The design load exceeds 10 kN, so this conditional Markdown block renders.</p>
 </blockquote>
 <div class="note">
  Pass
  <p>
   <span class="eq">
    <var>i</var>
    = 1
   </span>
  </p>
  of 3 — the HTML block repeats once per iteration.
 </div>
 <div class="note">
  Pass
  <p>
   <span class="eq">
    <var>i</var>
    = 2
   </span>
  </p>
  of 3 — the HTML block repeats once per iteration.
 </div>
 <div class="note">
  Pass
  <p>
   <span class="eq">
    <var>i</var>
    = 3
   </span>
  </p>
  of 3 — the HTML block repeats once per iteration.
 </div>
 <p class="note">
  Mode blocks nest inside
  <code>#if</code>
  .
 </p>
 <div class="note">Macros expand before parsing, so they work in every mode.</div>
 <p>
  Contrast:
  <code>#md on</code>
  stays in Calcpad mode and renders
  <strong>one comment line</strong>
  at a time.
 </p>
 <p>
  Contrast:
  <code>#markdown</code>
  renders whole blocks, with no
  <code>'</code>
  quotes.
 </p>
 <h2>Styled Markdown</h2>
 <p>
  The
  <code>&lt;style&gt;</code>
  block at the top of this file is the
  <strong>Markdown Elements - All</strong>
  CSS snippet, which covers what the report template leaves on browser defaults.
 </p>
 <blockquote>
  <p>A blockquote carries a left rule rather than a bare indent.</p>
 </blockquote>
 <p>
  Fenced blocks keep the language on
  <code>code.language-*</code>
  , though nothing
highlights them:
 </p>
 <pre><code class="language-text">E_d = 1.35 G + 1.5 Q
A   = 2 m * 3 m
</code></pre>
 <ol>
  <li>Ordered lists render alongside the bulleted ones above</li>
  <li>
   Inline
   <code>code</code>
   keeps a background of its own
  </li>
 </ol>
 <hr/>
 <p>A rule separates sections without needing a heading.</p>
 <h2>Links</h2>
 <p>
  An
  <code>&lt;img&gt;</code>
  in an
  <code>#html</code>
  or
  <code>#markdown</code>
  block resolves
  <code>{project}</code>
  and
  <code>{library}</code>
  the same way a
  <code>'</code>
  comment does.
 </p>
 <p>
  A bare URL autolinks in
  <code>#markdown</code>
  :
  <a href="https://calcpad-ce.org">https://calcpad-ce.org</a>
  — and so does
  <a href="https://github.com/imartincei/CalcpadCE">an explicit Markdown link</a>
  .
 </p>
 <p>
  Every link is confirmed before anything happens, because the target comes from
the worksheet.
 </p>
 <div class="note">
  <b>http / https</b>
  — prompts with the URL, then opens in the browser:
  <a href="https://github.com/imartincei/CalcpadCE">CalcpadCE on GitHub</a>
  <br/>
  <b>file</b>
  — prompts with the path, then opens with the system default.
    Must be absolute, so this one is machine-specific:
  <a href="file:///myfile.txt">Open file</a>
  <br/>
  <b>Other schemes are ignored</b>
  , since the app uses URLs for navigation:
  <a href="mailto:someone@example.com">mailto</a>
  ,
  <a href="javascript:alert('blocked')">javascript</a>
  <br/>
  <b>In-document anchors</b>
  scroll within the preview:
  <a href="#top">back to the top</a>
  <br/>
  <b>A quoted &gt; in an attribute</b>
  must not break the tag:
  <a href="https://example.com" title="Dead &gt; Live">load comparison</a>
 </div>
</div>
